      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "There seems to be consensus in #36759 to use `LogWarnThenDebug` when the Tor control port can't be reached as this makes such cases much less noisy. This pull aligns SOCKS5 proxies (`-proxy`, `-onion`) and the I2P SAM proxy (`-i2psam`) with that, making them also less noisy.\n\nUntil now every failed attempt logged the `connect()` failure at info level, and I2P additionally logged \"Couldn't listen\" as an error. Now the first failure is logged as a warning and later ones only at debug level.",
